<title>JAPAN: Gajoen ask-only under TSE surveillance.</title>
<headline>Gajoen ask-only under TSE surveillance.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Gajoen Kanko KK were ask-only in mid-morning on Tuesday after trading in the shares was put under surveillance by the Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE), brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0105 GMT, the shares were ask-only at 217 yen after closing at 257 yen on Friday.</p>
<p>Trading in the shares was suspended on Monday due to unclear details of tax-related issues.</p>
<p>The TSE said the shares were put under surveillance after the hotel operator admitted it had overdue taxes totalling about 13 billion yen, including taxes in arrears.</p>
